["<aside class=\"callout why\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>A plan ties the gun, the choke, the shell and the range together before the bird shows up. Then you only have to shoot.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Grouse plan card: 1 lead No. 7.5 or 6 is legal for grouse, 2 improved cylinder choke, 3 shots inside about 25 metres, 4 walk, stop, wait; the stop flushes the bird, 5 pattern this exact shell and choke first.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Grouse: the setup</text>\n<rect x=\"12\" y=\"44\" width=\"376\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n<circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"65.0\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"70.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text>\n<text x=\"54.0\" y=\"62.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\">Shell</text>\n<text x=\"54.0\" y=\"79.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Lead No. 7.5 or 6 (legal for grouse)</text>\n<rect x=\"12\" y=\"92\" width=\"376\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n<circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"113.0\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"118.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text>\n<text x=\"54.0\" y=\"110.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\">Choke</text>\n<text x=\"54.0\" y=\"127.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Improved cylinder</text>\n<rect x=\"12\" y=\"140\" width=\"376\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n<circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"161.0\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"166.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3</text>\n<text x=\"54.0\" y=\"158.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\">Range</text>\n<text x=\"54.0\" y=\"175.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Inside about 25 m (27 yd)</text>\n<rect x=\"12\" y=\"188\" width=\"376\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n<circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"209.0\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"214.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4</text>\n<text x=\"54.0\" y=\"206.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\">Walk, stop, wait</text>\n<text x=\"54.0\" y=\"223.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">The stop flushes the bird</text>\n<rect x=\"12\" y=\"236\" width=\"376\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n<circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"257.0\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"262.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">5</text>\n<text x=\"54.0\" y=\"254.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\">Pattern it</text>\n<text x=\"54.0\" y=\"271.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">This shell, this choke, 25 m</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>One setup for grouse, one for ducks. Write them on a card (Tip).</li><li>Hunting strategy lives in the species Masterclasses. This chapter is the shotgun side.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: where the strategy is</summary><ul><li>Grouse: <a href=\"#/s/mc-grouse-09\">How to hunt grouse</a>: walk the edges, stop, flush shooting, partner and dog.</li><li>Ducks: <a href=\"#/s/mc-ducks-09\">How to hunt ducks</a>: scouting, decoys, wind, calling, boat and kayak.</li><li>Geese: <a href=\"#/s/mc-geese-09\">How to hunt geese</a>: fields, layout blinds, flagging.</li><li>Your CZ 457 is also legal for grouse; the shotgun is for flushing birds (95%, <a href=\"#/s/mc-grouse-09/0\">Grouse Masterclass</a>).</li></ul></details>","<ul><li>Walk slow along edges, stop every 20 to 30 steps. The stop flushes the bird (Tip).</li><li>Swing through, keep moving, only with sky behind it (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: grouse with a shotgun</summary><ul><li>Most ruffed grouse shots come inside about 25 m (27 yd) through trees (Tip, <a href=\"#/s/mc-grouse-09/4\">Grouse Masterclass</a>).</li><li>Improved cylinder for close cover, modified for open country and late season <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>Lead No. 7.5 or 6 is legal for grouse <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. If you also hunt ducks that day, carry only steel (Tip).</li><li>Plug in: in BC a pump or semi auto must be plugged for grouse too (99%, page 12).</li><li>Carry: two hands, muzzle up, safety on, finger off. Safety off as the gun comes up (Tip).</li><li>Grouse seasons and limits near you: <a href=\"#/s/mc-grouse-10\">Grouse Masterclass rules</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Duck plan card: 1 steel No. 2 or 3, non toxic only, 2 improved cylinder or modified, steel rated, 3 shoot inside 35 metres, the farthest decoy, 4 plug in, 3 shells total, 5 pattern at 35 metres.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Ducks: the setup</text>\n<rect x=\"12\" y=\"44\" width=\"376\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n<circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"65.0\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#FF6A13\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"70.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text>\n<text x=\"54.0\" y=\"62.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\">Shell</text>\n<text x=\"54.0\" y=\"79.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Steel No. 2 or 3: non toxic only</text>\n<rect x=\"12\" y=\"92\" width=\"376\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n<circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"113.0\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"118.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text>\n<text x=\"54.0\" y=\"110.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\">Choke</text>\n<text x=\"54.0\" y=\"127.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">IC or modified, steel rated</text>\n<rect x=\"12\" y=\"140\" width=\"376\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n<circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"161.0\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"166.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3</text>\n<text x=\"54.0\" y=\"158.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\">Range</text>\n<text x=\"54.0\" y=\"175.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Inside 35 m (38 yd): far decoy</text>\n<rect x=\"12\" y=\"188\" width=\"376\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n<circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"209.0\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#FF6A13\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"214.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4</text>\n<text x=\"54.0\" y=\"206.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\">Plug in</text>\n<text x=\"54.0\" y=\"223.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">3 shells in the gun, total</text>\n<rect x=\"12\" y=\"236\" width=\"376\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n<circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"257.0\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"262.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">5</text>\n<text x=\"54.0\" y=\"254.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\">Pattern it</text>\n<text x=\"54.0\" y=\"271.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">This shell, this choke, 35 m</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Steel, steel rated choke, plug in, 35 m line (99% law; Tip on the rest).</li><li>Let birds commit. Shoot the ones inside your far decoy (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: ducks with a shotgun</summary><ul><li>Non toxic shot only, and none other in your pockets or boat (99%, s. 38(1)).</li><li>3 shells in the gun with the plug (99%, s. 37(1)(c)).</li><li>No slugs, one shotgun; any other gun unloaded and cased or taken apart (99%, s. 37).</li><li>Legal hours for ducks: half an hour before sunrise to half an hour after sunset (99%, s. 28(3)(b)).</li><li>Range: 35 m (38 yd) is a long shot with steel (70%, <a href=\"#/s/shotgun-skills/5\">Shotgun skills</a>).</li><li>Rules near Mission: <a href=\"#/s/rb-migratory-birds\">Migratory birds Rule Book</a>.</li></ul></details><aside class=\"callout warn\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Range card for a duck spread: put your farthest decoy at 35 metres. Birds inside it are in range; birds past it you watch, not shoot.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">The 35 metre decoy</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"260\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\"0.25\"/>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"250\" width=\"70\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#6b5a45\"/>\n<text x=\"45.0\" y=\"276.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">blind</text>\n<path d=\"M45 60 A210 210 0 0 1 255 270\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 6\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"100\" cy=\"220\" rx=\"12\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"140\" cy=\"200\" rx=\"12\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"120\" cy=\"244\" rx=\"12\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"170\" cy=\"232\" rx=\"12\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"150\" cy=\"170\" rx=\"12\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"193\" cy=\"122\" rx=\"12\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#FF6A13\"/>\n<line x1=\"245.9\" y1=\"134.0\" x2=\"200.0\" y2=\"124.0\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><circle cx=\"200.0\" cy=\"124.0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><rect x=\"245.9\" y=\"133.0\" width=\"128.2\" height=\"23.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"310.0\" y=\"150.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">far decoy: 35 m</text>\n<rect x=\"43.7\" y=\"112.0\" width=\"112.7\" height=\"24.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"100.0\" y=\"130.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">inside: shoot</text>\n<rect x=\"256.6\" y=\"62.0\" width=\"126.8\" height=\"24.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"320.0\" y=\"80.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">past it: watch</text>\n<line x1=\"60.0\" y1=\"255.0\" x2=\"178.1\" y2=\"136.0\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M182.0 132.0 L179.4 139.6 L174.5 134.7Z\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Range the farthest decoy at 35 m (38 yd) (Tip).</li><li>Inside it: shoot. Past it: watch (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why a range marker</summary><ul><li>Ducks look close because the eye judges by size; a marker keeps you honest (Tip).</li><li>Big ducks need about 100 pellets in the 76 cm circle at your longest range. That, not pellet energy, sets the limit (70%, <a href=\"#/s/shotgun-skills/5\">Shotgun skills</a>).</li><li>No dog yet: shorten your range. A sailed bird over big water is lost <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>You must make every reasonable effort to retrieve a bird you kill or wound (99%, <a href=\"#/s/mc-geese-09\">Geese Masterclass</a>).</li></ul></details>","<aside class=\"callout rule\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Grandpa's rule (wisdom): Decide your range in the truck. In the blind your eyes will lie to you.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Changing chokes in the blind instead of on paper.</li><li>Shooting the 45 m bird because the last one at 30 m fell.</li><li>Grouse shells and duck shells in one vest.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Write two cards: grouse (shell, choke, 25 m) and ducks (shell, choke, 35 m). Tape them inside your gun case lid.</p></aside>","<ul><li>Laws via the app Rule Book <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Tactics from the species Masterclasses (Tip, 60 to 70%). Checked 2026-10-23.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: all sources</summary><ul><li>Migratory Birds Regulations, 2022, ss. 28, 37, 38, via the app Rule Book <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li><li>BC synopsis page 12 plug rule, via the app Rule Book <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li><li><a href=\"#/s/mc-grouse-09\">Grouse Masterclass</a>, <a href=\"#/s/mc-ducks-09\">Duck Masterclass</a>, <a href=\"#/s/mc-geese-09\">Geese Masterclass</a>, <a href=\"#/s/shotgun-skills\">Shotgun skills</a> (60 to 70%, Tips labelled)</li></ul></details>"]